{
  "uid": "registration-case",
  "title": "Registration Case",
  "description": "Async registrations use RabbitMQ; sync calls the shared Registry processor directly. Separate HTTP response and Registry processing-to-commit graphs use milliseconds. The processing comparison uses the same boundary for both modes, including database connection waiting but excluding Rabbit queue waiting and downstream Compliance; concurrency can differ. One-second samples and refresh, 10-second rates, and rolling 30-second histogram p95 estimates. Lifetime counters reset independently on service restart.",
  "tags": [
    "registration-case"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "1s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 10,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-5m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Configuration and current activity",
      "description": "Configured limits are not measured busy work. Rabbit consumer count and prefetch apply only to async registrations; direct sync requests are bounded by shared HTTP admission and the database pool. Prefetch limits unfinished deliveries per Rabbit consumer. Both paths share Registry database connections. Virtual threads reports Registry thread mode. Compliance busy now includes database waiting and can remain nonzero after Registry has finished; useful Kafka concurrency is bounded by partition count.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(max(registry_config_consumers{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async Rabbit consumers",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(max(registry_config_prefetch{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async prefetch / consumer",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_max{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry pool max",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(max(registry_threads_virtual_enabled{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Virtual threads",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "expr": "(max(compliance_config_concurrency{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance consumers",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "F",
          "expr": "(sum(compliance_workers_active{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance busy now",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Virtual threads"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "OFF"
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "ON"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Server decisions and processing /s",
      "description": "Ten-second rate estimates from application counters sampled every second, not exact k6 burst throughput. Async accepted decisions follow RabbitMQ broker confirmation. Sync completed decisions follow a direct Registry transaction and include replays. Registry creations and Compliance checks count new committed results. These stages can finish at different times.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 3,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_intake_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"accepted\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async accepted decisions",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_sync_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=~\"created|replayed\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Sync completed decisions",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_registrations_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"created\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry creations",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(compliance_events_total{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\",outcome=\"processed\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance checks",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RabbitMQ queue (async only)",
      "description": "Sampled async messages in registration.commands. Direct sync requests do not enter this queue. Ready messages wait at the broker. Unacknowledged includes processing and prefetched deliveries waiting at Rabbit consumers, so it is not a busy-worker count. Ready and unacknowledged must both reach zero to drain. Missing telemetry remains a gap; sampled maxima can miss shorter peaks.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 3,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_ready{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Ready at broker",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_unacked{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Unacknowledged",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Registry processing and database pool",
      "description": "One-second samples. Processing registrations includes direct HTTP requests and Rabbit worker attempts, including time waiting for a database connection. This total is not bounded by Rabbit consumer count. Both paths share Hikari: active connections are borrowed; pending callers wait for one. Counts are not CPU parallelism. Short activity between samples can be missed.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_workers_active{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Processing registrations (HTTP + Rabbit)",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_active{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Active DB connections",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_pending{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Waiting for DB connection",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(hikaricp_connections_max{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Pool maximum",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Pool maximum"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    6,
                    4
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineWidth",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "HTTP response time (p95, milliseconds)",
      "description": "Successful HTTP responses over a rolling 30-second window. Async returns after RabbitMQ confirms acceptance; processing can continue afterward. Sync returns after its direct Registry transaction commits. These responses promise different things: a lower async response time does not mean a faster database write. Histogram estimates can differ from exact per-run k6 measurements. Idle windows remain gaps.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 12
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=\"/registrations\",method=\"POST\",status=\"202\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async: accepted into RabbitMQ (202)",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=\"/registrations/sync\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"200|201\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Sync: Registry DB committed (200/201)",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "axisLabel": "HTTP response (milliseconds)"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Async: accepted into RabbitMQ (202)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Sync: Registry DB committed (200/201)"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "yellow"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Registry processing to commit (p95, milliseconds)",
      "description": "The same timing boundary for both modes: processing starts on the HTTP thread or Rabbit worker and ends after the new user and outbox commit. Includes database connection waiting and transaction work. Excludes HTTP admission and normalization, Rabbit queue waiting and retry backoff, Kafka and Compliance. Only successful new registrations are recorded; replays and failures are excluded. Direct HTTP requests and Rabbit workers can still have different concurrency limits. Rolling 30-second histogram estimates can blend nearby runs. Idle windows and earlier runs remain gaps because this new metric has no historical backfill.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(registry_registration_processing_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",mode=\"sync\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Direct /sync: processing to commit",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(registry_registration_processing_seconds_bucket{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",mode=\"async\"}[30s])))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async worker: processing to commit",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left",
            "axisLabel": "Registry processing to commit (milliseconds)"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Direct /sync: processing to commit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "yellow"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Async worker: processing to commit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "width": 360
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Progress since each service started",
      "description": "Application decision and result counters since each service process started, not totals for the selected range or an exact per-run ledger. Async accepted and sync completed are server decisions; sync includes replay responses. Registry creations count new users, while Compliance checks count new results. Services reset independently on restart, so these values need not match. Use the HTML k6 report for a specific run.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_intake_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"accepted\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Async accepted",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_sync_requests_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=~\"created|replayed\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Sync completed",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_registrations_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",outcome=\"created\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry creations",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(compliance_events_total{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\",outcome=\"processed\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance checks",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Errors since each service started",
      "description": "Counters since each service started. HTTP 4xx/5xx includes validation errors, conflicts and 503 responses; a timeout can have an unknown outcome. Failed attempts can be retried. Dead-letter values count publishes, not current queue depth. Services reset independently. An absent HTTP error counter is zero only while Registry is UP; unavailable telemetry remains No data.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 37,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "((sum(http_server_requests_seconds_count{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=~\"/registrations(/sync)?\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"[45]..\"})) or on() vector(0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "HTTP 4xx/5xx",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_registrations_failures_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry failed attempts",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "(sum(registry_registrations_dead_lettered_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry dead letters",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "expr": "(sum(compliance_events_dead_lettered_total{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance dead letters",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "No data",
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Operational checks",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Scrape reachability",
      "description": "Prometheus scrape reachability only: UP means the metrics endpoint answered, not that registrations, Kafka or CDC are healthy. DOWN means a configured target failed its scrape. UNKNOWN means no up series exists for that job. No success guard hides DOWN states.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 18,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"registry\"}) or on() vector(-1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) or on() vector(-1)",
          "legendFormat": "Compliance",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) or on() vector(-1)",
          "legendFormat": "RabbitMQ",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": -1,
          "noValue": "UNKNOWN",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "-1": {
                  "text": "UNKNOWN",
                  "color": "gray"
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "DOWN",
                  "color": "red"
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "UP",
                  "color": "green"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": {
                "match": "null",
                "result": {
                  "text": "UNKNOWN",
                  "color": "gray"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "max": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "gray",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Registry DLQ depth (current)",
      "description": "Messages currently remaining in registration.commands.dlq: READY plus delivered/unacknowledged. This is current depth, not the lifetime dead-letter publication counter. Any positive depth is red. Missing queue series or an unreachable RabbitMQ scrape remain UNKNOWN; there is no zero fallback.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 42,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_ready{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands.dlq\"}) + sum(rabbitmq_queue_messages_unacked{job=\"rabbitmq\",queue=\"registration.commands.dlq\"})) and on() (max(up{job=\"rabbitmq\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "DLQ messages",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "noValue": "UNKNOWN",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "special",
              "options": {
                "match": "null",
                "result": {
                  "text": "UNKNOWN",
                  "color": "gray"
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Kafka fetch-position lag (records)",
      "description": "Sum of observed nonnegative client fetch-position lag for the exact topic outbox.event.user. This excludes dotted/underscored topic-label aliases and uses current lag, not rolling lag_max values. Fetch lag is not committed-offset lag or unfinished business work: zero does not prove every Compliance result committed. Missing, negative or NaN samples remain gaps, and an unreachable Compliance scrape hides stale values.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(kafka_consumer_fetch_manager_records_lag{job=\"compliance\",application=\"compliance-service\",topic=\"outbox.event.user\"} >= 0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"compliance\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Observed fetch-position lag",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left"
          },
          "noValue": "No data",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors per second",
      "description": "Ten-second rates, not lifetime totals or counts for one benchmark run. HTTP 5xx covers POST /registrations and /registrations/sync; Registry failed attempts count technical processing failures and can overlap HTTP failures or retried async work, so do not add the lines. Rates handle counter resets. HTTP error labels are created on first occurrence: rates need two samples and can undercount an initial short burst. The Registry failed-attempt counter is pre-initialized. An absent HTTP 5xx series is treated as zero only while Registry is UP; a failed scrape remains a gap.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "((sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\",uri=~\"/registrations(/sync)?\",method=\"POST\",status=~\"5..\"}[10s]))) or on() vector(0)) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "HTTP 5xx /s",
          "instant": false
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(registry_registrations_failures_total{job=\"registry\",application=\"registry-service\"}[10s]))) and on() (max(up{job=\"registry\"}) == 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Registry failed attempts /s",
          "instant": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 3,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisPlacement": "left"
          },
          "noValue": "No data",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "interval": "1s"
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "JVM diagnostics",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 55,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": true,
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": 15,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "JVM heap used (%)",
          "description": "Heap used as a percentage of the available reported heap maximum, separately for each application process. Used bytes include all heap pools; the denominator sums only positive maximums because G1 Eden/Survivor can report -1. Allocation and collection normally make this fluctuate; growth alone does not establish a leak. Missing memory metrics or an unreachable application scrape remain gaps.",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 56,
            "w": 12,
            "h": 9
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "targets": [
            {
              "refId": "A",
              "expr": "(100 * sum by (job) (jvm_memory_used_bytes{job=~\"registry|compliance\",area=\"heap\"}) / sum by (job) (jvm_memory_max_bytes{job=~\"registry|compliance\",area=\"heap\"} > 0)) and on(job) (max by (job) (up{job=~\"registry|compliance\"}) == 1)",
              "legendFormat": "{{job}} heap used",
              "instant": false
            }
          ],
          "fieldConfig": {
            "defaults": {
              "unit": "percent",
              "min": 0,
              "color": {
                "mode": "palette-classic"
              },
              "custom": {
                "drawStyle": "line",
                "lineInterpolation": "linear",
                "lineWidth": 2,
                "fillOpacity": 3,
                "showPoints": "never",
                "spanNulls": false,
                "axisCenteredZero": false,
                "axisPlacement": "left"
              },
              "noValue": "No data",
              "max": 100,
              "decimals": 1
            },
            "overrides": []
          },
          "options": {
            "legend": {
              "displayMode": "table",
              "placement": "bottom",
              "calcs": [
                "lastNotNull",
                "max"
              ]
            },
            "tooltip": {
              "mode": "multi",
              "sort": "desc"
            }
          },
          "interval": "1s"
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "type": "timeseries",
          "title": "GC pause time (%)",
          "description": "Percentage of wall-clock time recorded as GC pauses, averaged over 30 seconds for each application. Computed as 100 times the rate of cumulative jvm_gc_pause_seconds_sum. This is pause time, not CPU utilization and not an individual pause duration. Missing GC series or an unreachable application scrape remain gaps; no observations are invented.",
